---
import { Image } from 'astro:assets';
import BaseHead from '../components/BaseHead.astro';
import Footer from '../components/Footer.astro';
import Header from '../components/Header.astro';
import PhotoCredit from '../components/PhotoCredit.astro';
import depressedImage from '../assets/EmilyPhelan-Depressed.jpg';
import storyImage from '../assets/EmilyPhelan-London-YellowCard.jpg';
// The Cork jerseys photo, which fits this chapter. Swap if you have a
// better one from that era.
import corkImage from '../assets/801D4AC1-6CD8-453A-855F-0E1553ADB757.jpg';
import nowImage from '../assets/IMG_4060.jpeg';
import eighteenImage from '../assets/9d1c0198-216f-48a6-bd0f-178b9519da65.jpg';
import goodBitsImage from '../assets/695BB3EF-C6D5-4EAD-94F7-9DC225486BE8.jpg';
import covidImage from '../assets/IMG_4414-lc.jpg';
import londonImage from '../assets/1B8F435C-C301-4E03-BFC4-4837A3AE8E5B.jpg';
import differentHeadspaceImage from '../assets/EmilyPhelan-London-Playing-1.jpg';
import whyImage from '../assets/EmilyPhelan-Holloway-Playing.jpg';
import { SITE_TITLE } from '../consts';

const slides = [
  {
    images: [
      { src: storyImage, alt: 'Emily Phelan playing in London' },
    ],
    kicker: 'Introduction',
    title: 'My Story',
    paragraphs: [
      `My name is Emily. I am a 32-year-old female athlete living in London, and I play Ladies Gaelic Football for Holloway Gaels.`,
      `To be straight, I am not an expert or a psychologist, and I don't have this fully figured out. I still struggle with my mental health regularly.`,
      `Sport has always been a huge part of my life, but my journey with it has not been straightforward. I have struggled with anxiety and depression throughout my sporting career, and for a long time I did not have the language or the tools to understand what was happening in my own head. I didn't understand why pressure felt like too much sometimes or why my confidence could swing so much. I just knew I loved football, but I was also struggling in it.`,
    ],
  },
  {
    images: [
      { src: corkImage, alt: 'Emily Phelan playing underage for Cork' },
    ],
    kicker: 'Chapter 1',
    title: 'Walking Away',
    paragraphs: [
      `When I was a teenager, I played underage with Cork. I was captain of the under fourteens and played until I was 17, realistically on track for Cork senior. From the outside it probably looked like everything was going the right way.`,
      `Football was not the only sport I played, I played soccer for Cork and Munster and camogie with my club too. I was also on trial for Ireland in soccer, however I was marking Denise O'Sullivan and didn't make it lol. Sport was who I was, not just something I did. My mum was heavily involved in all of it, she loved sport as much as I did, and some of my best memories are tied up in that.`,
      `One day, I decided to walk away from sport entirely. Not because of injury, and not because I stopped being good enough. The pressure and the politics had built to a point where it was not fun anymore.`,
      `Selection played a part, being picked or dropped based on who you knew rather than how well you were playing. So did pressure from the sidelines, parents shouting and arguing about their children's ability, gossip about players and families around the club. I was pushed too hard, too young. Training loads and expectations felt more like senior inter-county than underage, and I was told I was the team's hope at 14. Missing the winning penalty in a quarter final of the All-Ireland at 16 left me feeling like I had failed everyone around me for weeks and weeks.`,
      `Some people might turn to another sport when they walk away from one. I didn't. It was seven years before I went back to sport at all. Burnout from football drove me towards alcohol and partying instead, towards the freedom of doing what I wanted, when I wanted. That pressure was never dealt with, it followed me around in other shapes. Walking away did not solve it. It only delayed it.`,
    ],
  },
  {
    images: [
      { src: eighteenImage, alt: 'Emily Phelan in her late teens' },
      { src: goodBitsImage, alt: 'Emily Phelan travelling in her twenties' },
    ],
    kicker: 'Chapter 2',
    title: "Early 20's",
    paragraphs: [
      `From 18 to 25 I was drinking heavily. I gained a lot of weight and my confidence got worse with it, which made me want to go out and drink more, which made all of it worse again. I spent years battling anxiety and depression, but I wouldn't have called it that at the time, I would have blamed the hangover, or stress from studying or work.`,
      `I was rarely sober during university, and then I went to Whistler where I wasn't sober at all. Looking back, I can't think of many weeks where drinking wasn't part of most days, not just weekends.`,
      `Some of that pressure eased during this time. The people I met along the way only knew that version of me, they didn't hold me to a higher standard. I was just Emily to them, not captain, not the girl who was supposed to make it, not anyone's hope for anything. I went to concerts, festivals, I skied, and for a few years life felt lighter. I am so grateful to those friends who were part of that journey, they are still some of my closest friends today.`,
      `I was also a high achiever through all of this. I did well academically, and I have a very solid career today.`,
      `Looking back though, the travelling and the whole business of enjoying my twenties put a blanket over the anxiety and the depression. It did not deal with any of it. It just covered it up well enough that I could keep going.`,
    ],
  },
  {
    images: [
      { src: covidImage, alt: 'Emily Phelan during the Covid years' },
    ],
    kicker: 'Chapter 3',
    title: 'Covid Took the Blanket Off',
    paragraphs: [
      `Then the travelling stopped. I came home to Cork to do my masters, working part-time alongside it, with every intention of travelling again once I finished.`,
      `I went back to football. I focused on losing weight and getting back into football as a distraction. I became obsessed with it, went vegetarian to lose weight. But everything was always just a distraction, I became obsessed with things because they gave me something else to focus on.`,
      `Then Covid hit, and I was trapped.`,
      `I became very unhappy. I was having panic attacks on the pitch. I was still drinking, and I spent a lot of time depressed in bed. I struggled through years of blaming everyone else for it, I blamed my family, I blamed football, I blamed Cork and my hometown for making me unhappy.`,
      `I met my partner during this time, and naturally things didn't work out, because I put all my faith in him making my life better rather than doing that work myself.`,
      `But the problem was never my home, or my family, or football. It was me, and my inability to face my anxiety and depression.`,
      `So I ran away to London hoping I would build a happy life for myself. At times I genuinely did. I worked, I skied, I partied. I enjoyed my life. But I was a ticking timebomb.`,
      `I joined Holloway Gaels and this brought the anxiety back. The heightened pressure from football made things worse for me, and because I did not know football was a trigger, I just kept having panic attacks and long spells of depression without understanding why.`,
      `I became obsessed with my weight and how I looked, deeply insecure about it. I never used to be able to go to training without my makeup on, and then I would always be fidgeting with my football gear, wondering if someone was looking at my weight, or judging how I looked when I was playing, or judging if I was good enough.`,
    ],
  },
  {
    images: [
      { src: depressedImage, alt: 'Emily Phelan on league final day' },
    ],
    kicker: 'Chapter 4',
    title: 'Hitting Rock Bottom',
    paragraphs: [
      `Number 18 is me on league final day. I remember feeling happy for my team, but I could not fully feel it for myself because I was so caught up in my own performance. I was not in a good place and that showed on the pitch.`,
      `What I understand now, looking back, is that it was not just performance anxiety. I was dealing with undiagnosed anxiety and depression and it spilled over into everything, not just my sport.`,
      `Everything felt heavier than it should have, and it kept getting worse. Not just games, but life in general. There were days that felt harder than the last, times I felt really low for no clear reason, and panic attacks I did not fully understand. My mind was constantly busy. I was overthinking, second-guessing myself, never fully present in the moment. Afterwards, I would replay everything in my head over and over, feeling disconnected from what had just happened.`,
      `My thoughts became very negative, and I continued to blame others for how I was feeling.`,
      `It didn't happen all at once. I was drinking heavily and having panic attacks constantly, not just before big games but out of nowhere, in the middle of ordinary days. I had a panic attack on the pitch, mid-match, in front of everyone, and had no idea how to explain what had just happened to me or why.`,
      `There were stretches where I couldn't get out of bed for days on end. Not tired, not hungover in the normal sense, just unable to physically make myself move. My job was suffering because of it. I was missing things, underperforming, running on nothing, and too ashamed to tell anyone why.`,
      `Eventually I hit rock bottom. My thoughts started to get darker and darker, to the point where I was worried for my own safety. I went to my doctor and was put on medication, and for the first time in 15 years my head went silent.`,
      `That was when I realised how loud it had been. The overthinking had started when I was a teenager, and I had carried it for so long that I thought it was normal. I just did not know.`,
      `Getting the right help was the turning point. It gave me space to think clearly, and from there I could finally start doing the work on the mental side of my sport and my life.`,
    ],
  },
  {
    images: [
      { src: nowImage, alt: 'Emily Phelan with a cup' },
    ],
    kicker: 'Chapter 5',
    title: 'Where I Am Now',
    paragraphs: [
      `At the time of writing this, I am 47 days sober. I want to be honest about that because I know people might look at me and not think I had a problem. But I did.`,
      `Once I started drinking, I did not have the ability to stop. My anxiety and depression eased in that moment, and I craved holding onto that feeling for as long as possible. But that led to blackouts nine times out of ten, and a lot of regrets.`,
      `I ended up seeking help for the drinking. The medication helped me silence my mind enough to know I needed to stop drinking if I wanted the anxiety and depression to be manageable. I went through years of using alcohol as a crutch, and I am still working through it now, one day at a time.`,
      `I still overthink everything, whether I am good enough or fit enough or will I be dropped. I still have weeks where my head is hard work. The difference is that I know what it is now, and I know what helps, even when I am still in the middle of figuring it out.`,
      `It took a lot of work, a lot of learning, and a lot of uncomfortable reflection on how I was thinking, feeling, and showing up in life and in sport. Mind the Gael is the platform I wish I had when I was younger, the language, the tools, and the honest stories that would have helped me understand my own head much sooner.`,
      `This website was created in the hope that my experience helps at least one person not go through the struggles I went through.`,
    ],
  },
];

// The page is a grid of players, not one long carousel. Emily's story is one
// square tile among several; clicking it opens the chapters in a dialog.
// That leaves room on the page for other players as their stories come in,
// which a full-width six-chapter carousel did not.
//
// To add a player: give them a `chapters` array in the same shape as
// `slides` above and drop `placeholder: true`.
type Player = {
  name: string;
  blurb: string;
  cover?: ImageMetadata;
  coverAlt?: string;
  chapters: typeof slides;
  placeholder: boolean;
};

const players: Player[] = [
  {
    name: 'Emily Phelan',
    blurb: 'Cork underage, seven years out of sport, then Holloway Gaels. Anxiety, depression, drinking, and what helped.',
    cover: storyImage,
    coverAlt: 'Emily Phelan playing in London',
    chapters: slides,
    placeholder: false,
  },
  {
    name: 'Player story',
    blurb: '',
    chapters: [],
    placeholder: true,
  },
  {
    name: 'Player story',
    blurb: '',
    chapters: [],
    placeholder: true,
  },
  {
    name: 'Player story',
    blurb: 'Want yours here? Email emilyphelan@mindthegael.co.uk',
    chapters: [],
    placeholder: true,
  },
];
---

<!doctype html>
<html lang="en">
  <head>
    <BaseHead title={`About | ${SITE_TITLE}`} description="My Story - Emily Phelan's journey through anxiety, depression, and finding mental performance tools for sport." />
  </head>
  <body class="about-page">
    <Header />
    <main class="about-layout">
      <section class="about-intro">
        <h1>Player Stories</h1>
        <p class="about-intro-sub">Tap a player to read her story.</p>
      </section>

      <section class="player-grid-wrap" aria-label="Player stories">
        <ul class="player-grid">
          {players.map((player, playerIndex) => (
            <li class:list={["player-tile", { "player-tile-placeholder": player.placeholder }]}>
              {player.placeholder ? (
                <div class="player-tile-inner" aria-disabled="true">
                  <div class="player-cover player-cover-empty" aria-hidden="true">
                    <span class="player-cover-mark">TBC</span>
                  </div>
                  <h2 class="player-name">{player.name}</h2>
                  {player.blurb && <p class="player-blurb">{player.blurb}</p>}
                </div>
              ) : (
                <button
                  type="button"
                  class="player-tile-inner player-tile-button"
                  data-player={playerIndex}
                  aria-label={`Read ${player.name}'s story, ${player.chapters.length} chapters`}
                >
                  <span class="player-cover">
                    {player.cover && (
                      <Image
                        src={player.cover}
                        alt=""
                        class="player-cover-img"
                        loading="eager"
                        widths={[300, 500, 700]}
                        sizes="(max-width: 700px) 45vw, 260px"
                      />
                    )}
                  </span>
                  <span class="player-name">{player.name}</span>
                  <span class="player-blurb">{player.blurb}</span>
                  <span class="player-cta">Read her story ({player.chapters.length} chapters)</span>
                </button>
              )}
            </li>
          ))}
        </ul>
      </section>

      {/* One dialog per player with a story, holding her chapters. Hidden
          until the tile is clicked. A native <dialog> so the browser traps
          focus, handles Escape and hides the page behind it. */}
      {players.map((player, playerIndex) => (
        !player.placeholder && (
          <dialog class="story-dialog" data-player-dialog={playerIndex} aria-label={`${player.name}'s story`}>
            <div class="story-dialog-panel">
              <div class="story-dialog-bar">
                <p class="story-dialog-title">{player.name}</p>
                <button type="button" class="story-dialog-close" aria-label="Close">Done</button>
              </div>

              <div class="story-dialog-body">
                {player.chapters.map((chapter) => (
                  <article class="chapter">
                    <div class="chapter-images" data-count={chapter.images.length}>
                      {chapter.images.map((img) => (
                        <div class="chapter-image-item">
                          <Image
                            src={img.src}
                            alt={img.alt}
                            class="chapter-image"
                            loading="lazy"
                            widths={[400, 600, 900]}
                            sizes={chapter.images.length > 1 ? "45vw" : "(max-width: 900px) 100vw, 480px"}
                          />
                          <PhotoCredit src={img.src.src} class="on-white" />
                        </div>
                      ))}
                    </div>
                    <p class="chapter-kicker">{chapter.kicker}</p>
                    <h3 class="chapter-title">{chapter.title}</h3>
                    {chapter.paragraphs.map((p) => <p class="chapter-text">{p}</p>)}
                  </article>
                ))}
              </div>
            </div>
          </dialog>
        )
      ))}
    </main>
    <Footer />

    <script is:inline>
      (() => {
        // Tile opens the matching dialog. showModal() rather than a class
        // toggle so focus is trapped, Escape closes, and the grid behind is
        // hidden from screen readers while the story is open.
        document.querySelectorAll('.player-tile-button').forEach((tile) => {
          const index = tile.dataset.player;
          const dialog = document.querySelector('[data-player-dialog="' + index + '"]');
          if (!dialog) return;

          tile.addEventListener('click', () => {
            dialog.showModal();
            document.body.classList.add('story-open');
            // Long stories open scrolled to wherever the last visit left
            // them otherwise.
            dialog.querySelector('.story-dialog-body').scrollTop = 0;
            dialog.querySelector('.story-dialog-close').focus();
          });

          // Click on the backdrop, outside the panel, closes it.
          dialog.addEventListener('click', (event) => {
            if (event.target === dialog) dialog.close();
          });

          dialog.querySelector('.story-dialog-close').addEventListener('click', () => dialog.close());
          dialog.addEventListener('close', () => document.body.classList.remove('story-open'));
        });
      })();
    </script>
  </body>
</html>

<style>
  .about-layout {
    padding: 0;
    background: var(--green-dark);
    min-height: calc(100vh - 220px);
  }

  /* ── Intro ── */
  .about-intro {
    text-align: center;
    padding: 3rem 1.5rem 1.5rem;
    color: var(--green-light);
  }

  .about-intro-kicker {
    text-transform: uppercase;
    letter-spacing: 0.16em;
    font-size: 0.78rem;
    font-weight: 700;
    color: var(--purple);
    margin: 0 0 0.6rem;
  }

  .about-intro h1 {
    margin: 0 0 0.7rem;
    color: var(--green-lime);
    font-size: clamp(1.8rem, 4vw, 2.8rem);
    line-height: 1.15;
  }

  .about-intro-sub {
    margin: 0;
    color: var(--green-light);
    opacity: 0.78;
    font-size: 0.95rem;
  }

  /* ── Player grid ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────
     A square tile per player rather than one full-width carousel of my own
     chapters. The carousel gave the whole page to one story and left
     nowhere for anyone else; this scales as players come in. */
  .player-grid-wrap {
    max-width: 1100px;
    margin: 0 auto;
    padding: 0 1.5rem 4rem;
  }

  .player-grid {
    list-style: none;
    padding: 0;
    margin: 0;
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fill, minmax(230px, 1fr));
    gap: 1.25rem;
  }

  .player-tile-inner {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: 0.5rem;
    width: 100%;
    height: 100%;
    padding: 0.85rem 0.85rem 1rem;
    border: 2px solid rgba(105, 0, 90, 0.35);
    border-top: 6px solid var(--purple);
    border-radius: 14px;
    background: #ffffff;
    font: inherit;
    text-align: left;
    box-shadow: 0 10px 24px rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.3);
  }

  .player-tile-button {
    cursor: pointer;
    transition: transform 0.18s ease, box-shadow 0.18s ease;
  }

  .player-tile-button:hover {
    transform: translateY(-4px);
    box-shadow: 0 18px 34px rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.4);
  }

  .player-tile-button:focus-visible {
    outline: 3px solid var(--green-lime);
    outline-offset: 3px;
  }

  /* Square, so the grid reads as a set of equal players rather than
     ranking them by however tall their photo happens to be. */
  .player-cover {
    display: block;
    width: 100%;
    aspect-ratio: 1 / 1;
    border-radius: 10px;
    overflow: hidden;
    background: #f4ecf7;
  }

  .player-cover-img {
    width: 100%;
    height: 100%;
    object-fit: cover;
    object-position: center 20%;
    display: block;
  }

  .player-cover-empty {
    display: flex;
    align-items: center;
    justify-content: center;
    border: 2px dashed rgba(105, 0, 90, 0.3);
    background: repeating-linear-gradient(
      135deg,
      rgba(105, 0, 90, 0.05) 0 10px,
      transparent 10px 20px
    );
  }

  .player-cover-mark {
    color: rgba(105, 0, 90, 0.5);
    font-size: 1.4rem;
    font-weight: 800;
    letter-spacing: 0.18em;
  }

  .player-name {
    display: block;
    margin: 0;
    color: var(--purple);
    font-size: 1.05rem;
    font-weight: 800;
    line-height: 1.25;
  }

  .player-blurb {
    display: block;
    margin: 0;
    color: #1a1a1a;
    opacity: 0.82;
    font-size: 0.88rem;
    line-height: 1.45;
    /* The invite blurb carries an email address, which is one long
       unbreakable token and runs out past the tile edge without this. */
    overflow-wrap: anywhere;
  }

  .player-cta {
    display: block;
    margin-top: auto;
    padding-top: 0.5rem;
    color: var(--purple);
    font-size: 0.82rem;
    font-weight: 700;
  }

  /* Empty slots sit flat and dashed on the dark page, so they read as
     "nobody here yet" rather than as a card that failed to load. */
  .player-tile-placeholder .player-tile-inner {
    background: none;
    border: 1px dashed rgba(192, 254, 113, 0.3);
    box-shadow: none;
  }

  .player-tile-placeholder .player-name {
    color: var(--green-light);
  }

  .player-tile-placeholder .player-blurb {
    color: var(--green-light);
    opacity: 0.7;
  }

  /* ── Story dialog ── */
  .story-dialog {
    width: min(760px, 94vw);
    max-height: 90vh;
    padding: 0;
    border: none;
    border-radius: 18px;
    background: transparent;
    overflow: visible;
  }

  .story-dialog::backdrop {
    background: rgba(3, 10, 6, 0.78);
  }

  .story-dialog-panel {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    max-height: 90vh;
    border-radius: 18px;
    border-top: 7px solid var(--purple);
    background: #ffffff;
    overflow: hidden;
  }

  /* Sticky bar, because the stories run long and Done should not require
     scrolling back to the top. */
  .story-dialog-bar {
    display: flex;
    align-items: center;
    justify-content: space-between;
    gap: 1rem;
    padding: 0.9rem 1.2rem;
    border-bottom: 1px solid rgba(105, 0, 90, 0.2);
    background: #ffffff;
  }

  .story-dialog-title {
    margin: 0;
    color: var(--purple);
    font-size: 1.05rem;
    font-weight: 800;
  }

  .story-dialog-close {
    padding: 0.45rem 0.9rem;
    border: 2px solid var(--purple);
    border-radius: 999px;
    background: var(--purple);
    color: #ffffff;
    font: inherit;
    font-weight: 700;
    cursor: pointer;
  }

  .story-dialog-close:focus-visible {
    outline: 3px solid var(--green-lime);
    outline-offset: 2px;
  }

  .story-dialog-body {
    padding: 1.4rem 1.5rem 2rem;
    overflow-y: auto;
    color: #1a1a1a;
  }

  .chapter + .chapter {
    margin-top: 2.2rem;
    padding-top: 2rem;
    border-top: 1px solid rgba(105, 0, 90, 0.15);
  }

  .chapter-images {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    align-items: center;
    gap: 0.9rem;
    margin-bottom: 1rem;
  }

  .chapter-image-item {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    align-items: center;
  }

  /* Every chapter image is the same size, whether the chapter has one
     photo or two. Two-up chapters used to shrink to 47% and 220px tall,
     which made the skiing and festival photos far smaller than the ones
     either side of them. Two photos stack instead. */
  .chapter-image {
    width: auto;
    max-width: 100%;
    max-height: 360px;
    height: auto;
    border-radius: 10px;
    display: block;
  }

  .chapter-kicker {
    margin: 0 0 0.3rem;
    color: var(--purple);
    text-transform: uppercase;
    letter-spacing: 0.14em;
    font-size: 0.74rem;
    font-weight: 800;
  }

  .chapter-title {
    margin: 0 0 0.9rem;
    color: var(--purple);
    font-size: 1.5rem;
    line-height: 1.2;
  }

  .chapter-text {
    margin: 0 0 1rem;
    color: #1a1a1a;
    font-size: 1.01rem;
    line-height: 1.65;
  }

  /* Stop the page behind the dialog scrolling on iOS. */
  :global(body.story-open) {
    overflow: hidden;
  }

  @media (max-width: 720px) {
    .player-grid-wrap { padding: 0 1rem 3rem; }
    /* One per row on a phone. Two 150px tiles side by side left the name
       and blurb about four words wide. */
    .player-grid { grid-template-columns: 1fr; gap: 0.9rem; }
    .player-cover { aspect-ratio: 16 / 10; }
    .story-dialog-body { padding: 1.1rem 1.1rem 1.6rem; }
    .chapter-title { font-size: 1.25rem; }
  }

</style>